==Visa requirements==
South Ossetia has mutual visa-free agreements with [[Russia|Russia in 2010]]<ref>{{Cite web |title=Соглашение между Правительством Республики Южная Осетия и Правительством Российской Федерации о взаимных безвизовых поездках граждан Республики Южная Осетия и Российской Федерации {{!}} Министерство иностранных дел Республики Южная Осетия |url=https://mfa.rsogov.org/ru/node/1209 |access-date=2022-06-05 |website=mfa.rsogov.org}}</ref> and [[Abkhazia|Abkhazia in 2015]].<ref>[http://apsnypress.info/en/news/abkhazia-and-south-ossetia-have-entered-visa-free-travel-regime/ Abkhazia and South Ossetia have entered visa-free travel regime]</ref> South Ossetians can either use their domestic or international passport to enter Russia and Abkhazia. In 2016, news reports claimed that South Ossetia and [[Venezuela]] were preparing to sign a mutual visa-free agreement.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.linxtter.com/front/news-details.php?sdk=188 |title=Abkhazia And Venezuela Arranging For Visa-free Travel — Foreign Minister - RA |access-date=2016-05-02 |archive-date=2016-06-03 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160603102949/http://www.linxtter.com/front/news-details.php?sdk=188 |url-status=dead }}</ref> It is unknown if an agreement was ever signed.

